{"id":"mahabharata-7-059","work":"mahabharata","part":7,"partName":"द्रोणपर्व","partNameEn":"Drona Parva","unit":59,"title":"एकोनषष्टितमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 59 · Yudhishthira and Krishna","summary":{"en":"Yudhishthira greets Krishna, saying the Pandavas depend on him alone as the gods on Indra for victory. Krishna assures him that Arjuna will kill Jayadratha that day and that he should lose his grief.","kn":"ಯುಧಿಷ್ಠಿರ ಕೃಷ್ಣನನ್ನು ಸ್ವಾಗತಿಸಿ, ಇಂದ್ರನ ಮೇಲೆ ದೇವತೆಗಳಂತೆ ಪಾಂಡವರು ಜಯಕ್ಕಾಗಿ ಅವನನ್ನೇ ಆಶ್ರಯಿಸಿದ್ದಾರೆಂದು ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಅರ್ಜುನ ಅಂದೇ ಜಯದ್ರಥನನ್ನು ಕೊಲ್ಲುವನೆಂದೂ ದುಃಖ ಬಿಡಬೇಕೆಂದೂ ಕೃಷ್ಣ ಭರವಸೆ ನೀಡುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"युधिष्ठिर कृष्ण का स्वागत करते हैं और कहते हैं कि इन्द्र पर देवताओं की तरह पाण्डव विजय के लिए उन्हीं पर निर्भर हैं। कृष्ण आश्वासन देते हैं कि अर्जुन उसी दिन जयद्रथ को मारेंगे और शोक त्याग दें।","te":"యుధిష్ఠిరుడు కృష్ణుని స్వాగతించి ఇంద్రునిపై దేవతల్లా జయానికి పాండవులు ఆయననే ఆశ్రయిస్తారని అంటాడు. అర్జునుడు ఆ రోజే జయద్రథుని చంపుతాడని, దుఃఖం వీడమని కృష్ణుడు హామీ ఇస్తాడు.","ta":"யுதிஷ்டிரர் கண்ணனை வரவேற்று, இந்திரனைத் தேவர் போல் வெற்றிக்குப் பாண்டவர் அவரையே நம்புகின்றனர் என்கிறார். அர்ஜுனன் அன்றே ஜயத்ரதனைக் கொல்வான் என்றும் துயரத்தை விடவேண்டும் என்றும் கண்ணன் உறுதியளிக்கிறார்.","ml":"യുധിഷ്ഠിരൻ കൃഷ്ണനെ സ്വാഗതം ചെയ്യുന്നു; ദേവന്മാർ വിജയത്തിനായി ഇന്ദ്രനെ ആശ്രയിക്കുന്നതുപോലെ പാണ്ഡവർ അദ്ദേഹത്തെ മാത്രം ആശ്രയിക്കുന്നുവെന്ന് പറയുന്നു. ആ ദിവസം അർജുനൻ ജയദ്രഥനെ വധിക്കുമെന്നും ദുഃഖം ഉപേക്ഷിക്കണമെന്നും കൃഷ്ണൻ ഉറപ്പ് നൽകുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 7.59; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Tue Sep 22 2026","sections":[{"title":"प्रतिज्ञापर्व","titleEn":"Pratijna Parva (Arjuna's vow)","verses":[{"text":"युधिष्ठिर उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"सुखेन रजनी व्युष्टा कच्चित्ते मधुसूदन ।\nकच्चिज्ज्ञानानि सर्वाणि प्रसन्नानि तवाच्युत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Madhusudana, has your night passed happily? Achyuta, are all your faculties serene?"}},{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":2,"text":"वासुदेवोऽपि तद्युक्तं पर्यपृच्छद्युधिष्ठिरम् ।\nततः क्षत्ता प्रकृतयो न्यवेदयदुपस्थिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Vasudeva too asked Yudhishthira the fitting questions. Then the doorkeeper announced that the people who had come were waiting."}},{"n":3,"text":"अनुज्ञातश्च राज्ञा स प्रावेशयत तं जनम् ।\nविराटं भीमसेनं च धृष्टद्युम्नं च सात्यकिम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"With the king's leave, he brought in those people: Virata, Bhimasena, Dhrishtadyumna and Satyaki,"}},{"n":4,"text":"शिखण्डिनं यमौ चैव चेकितानं च केकयान् ।\nयुयुत्सुं चैव कौरव्यं पाञ्चाल्यं चोत्तमौजसम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Shikhandin, the twins, Chekitana, the Kekayas, Yuyutsu of the Kaurava line, and the Panchala Uttamaujas."}},{"n":5,"text":"एते चान्ये च बहवः क्षत्रियाः क्षत्रियर्षभम् ।\nउपतस्थुर्महात्मानं विविशुश्चासनेषु ते ॥","meaning":{"en":"These and many other kshatriyas came to attend that great-souled bull among kshatriyas, and took their seats."}},{"n":6,"text":"एकस्मिन्नासने वीरावुपविष्टौ महाबलौ ।\nकृष्णश्च युयुधानश्च महात्मानौ महाद्युती ॥","meaning":{"en":"The two mighty heroes, great-souled and brilliant, Krishna and Yuyudhana, sat together on one seat."}},{"n":7,"text":"ततो युधिष्ठिरस्तेषां शृण्वतां मधुसूदनम् ।\nअब्रवीत्पुण्डरीकाक्षमाभाष्य मधुरं वचः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Yudhishthira, addressing the lotus-eyed Madhusudana in the hearing of all of them, spoke sweet words."}},{"n":8,"text":"एकं त्वां वयमाश्रित्य सहस्राक्षमिवामराः ।\nप्रार्थयामो जयं युद्धे शाश्वतानि सुखानि च ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Relying on you alone, as the gods rely on the thousand-eyed Indra, we ask for victory in battle and lasting happiness.\""}},{"n":9,"text":"त्वं हि राज्यविनाशं च द्विषद्भिश्च निराक्रियाम् ।\nक्लेशांश्च विविधान्कृष्ण सर्वांस्तानपि वेत्थ नः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Krishna, you know the loss of our kingdom, our rejection by our enemies and our many kinds of suffering, all of them.\""}},{"n":10,"text":"त्वयि सर्वेश सर्वेषामस्माकं भक्तवत्सल ।\nसुखमायत्तमत्यर्थं यात्रा च मधुसूदन ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Lord of all, kind to devotees, Madhusudana, the happiness of all of us and our whole journey depend greatly on you.\""}},{"n":11,"text":"स तथा कुरु वार्ष्णेय यथा त्वयि मनो मम ।\nअर्जुनस्य यथा सत्या प्रतिज्ञा स्याच्चिकीर्षिता ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"So act, descendant of Vrishni, in a way that my mind rests on you and that Arjuna's vow may be made true as he wishes.\""}},{"n":12,"text":"स भवांस्तारयत्वस्माद्दुःखामर्षमहार्णवात् ।\nपारं तितीर्षतामद्य प्लवो नो भव माधव ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Carry us across this great ocean of grief and anger. Madhava, be our raft today as we try to reach the far shore.\""}},{"n":13,"text":"न हि तत्कुरुते संख्ये कार्तवीर्यसमस्त्वपि ।\nरथी यत्कुरुते कृष्ण सारथिर्यत्नमास्थितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Even a warrior equal to Kartavirya cannot do in battle what a charioteer does when he exerts himself, Krishna.\""}},{"text":"वासुदेव उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vasudeva said:"}},{"n":14,"text":"सामरेष्वपि लोकेषु सर्वेषु न तथाविधः ।\nशरासनधरः कश्चिद्यथा पार्थो धनंजयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"In all the worlds, even among the gods, there is no wielder of the bow like Partha Dhananjaya.\""}},{"n":15,"text":"वीर्यवानस्त्रसंपन्नः पराक्रान्तो महाबलः ।\nयुद्धशौण्डः सदामर्षी तेजसा परमो नृणाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"He is strong, rich in weapons, bold, of great might, a champion in battle, always intolerant of insult and the foremost of men in splendour.\""}},{"n":16,"text":"स युवा वृषभस्कन्धो दीर्घबाहुर्महाबलः ।\nसिंहर्षभगतिः श्रीमान्द्विषतस्ते हनिष्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"That young man with the shoulders of a bull, long arms and great strength, with the gait of a lion or a bull, glorious, will kill your enemies.\""}},{"n":17,"text":"अहं च तत्करिष्यामि यथा कुन्तीसुतोऽर्जुनः ।\nधार्तराष्ट्रस्य सैन्यानि धक्ष्यत्यग्निरिवोत्थितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"I too shall do so, so that Arjuna, son of Kunti, will burn the armies of Dhritarashtra's son like a risen fire.\""}},{"n":18,"text":"अद्य तं पापकर्माणं क्षुद्रं सौभद्रघातिनम् ।\nअपुनर्दर्शनं मार्गमिषुभिः क्षेप्स्यतेऽर्जुनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Today Arjuna will fling that sinful, petty killer of Subhadra's son onto the road from which there is no return, with his arrows.\""}},{"n":19,"text":"तस्याद्य गृध्राः श्येनाश्च वडगोमायवस्तथा ।\nभक्षयिष्यन्ति मांसानि ये चान्ये पुरुषादकाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Today vultures, hawks, herons, jackals and other flesh-eaters will devour his flesh.\""}},{"n":20,"text":"यद्यस्य देवा गोप्तारः सेन्द्राः सर्वे तथाप्यसौ ।\nराजधानीं यमस्याद्य हतः प्राप्स्यति संकुले ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Even if all the gods with Indra were his protectors, once killed he will reach the crowded capital of Yama today.\""}},{"n":21,"text":"निहत्य सैन्धवं जिष्णुरद्य त्वामुपयास्यति ।\nविशोको विज्वरो राजन्भव भूतिपुरस्कृतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Having killed Saindhava, Jishnu will come to you today. King, be free of sorrow and fever, and be led by good fortune.\""}}]}]}